   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "What is \\( \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\cos^2 x + \\cos x - 2}{\\cos^2 x - 1} \\)?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         3,
         2
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "At x = 0, cos x = 1, so the numerator is 1 + 1 - 2 = 0 and the denominator is 1 - 1 = 0, and the quotient is zero over zero.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Treat cos x as the variable and factor: cos^2 x + cos x - 2 = (cos x - 1)(cos x + 2) and cos^2 x - 1 = (cos x - 1)(cos x + 1).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  [
                     "Cos",
                     "x"
                  ],
                  1
               ],
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Cos",
                     "x"
                  ],
                  2
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  [
                     "Cos",
                     "x"
                  ],
                  1
               ],
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Cos",
                     "x"
                  ],
                  1
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "For x near 0 with x not equal to 0, cos x is not 1, so the factor cos x - 1 divides out, leaving (cos x + 2)/(cos x + 1).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Cos",
                  "x"
               ],
               2
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Cos",
                  "x"
               ],
               1
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The simplified expression is continuous at 0, so the limit is (1 + 2)/(1 + 1) = 3/2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            2
         ]
      }
   ],
